; Probe a block of 3 x 2 points
;
; ORs the tile flags of six cells into E (E starts at 0): (x+B, y+C), (x+B+3, y+C), (x+B+6, y+C), then the same three
; one cell row lower (y+C+4), the last three right to left. The crouching branch of #R$A8A5 uses it to find harmful
; tiles. B is unchanged, C is left increased by 4.
; .
; Hardware: none; reads the tile flag map.
;
; HL Position: H = x, L = y (2-pixel units)
; B Offset of the first point in x
; C Offset of the first point in y
; D Column mask (always $1F)
; O:E OR of the tile flags at the points
; O:C C + 4
@label=ProbeBlock3x2
c$A990 LD E,$00   ;
 $A992 CALL $A9FE ;
 $A995 INC B      ;
 $A996 INC B      ;
 $A997 INC B      ;
 $A998 CALL $A9FE ;
 $A99B INC B      ;
 $A99C INC B      ;
 $A99D INC B      ;
 $A99E CALL $A9FE ;
 $A9A1 INC C      ;
 $A9A2 INC C      ;
 $A9A3 INC C      ;
 $A9A4 INC C      ;
 $A9A5 CALL $A9FE ;
 $A9A8 DEC B      ;
 $A9A9 DEC B      ;
 $A9AA DEC B      ;
 $A9AB CALL $A9FE ;
 $A9AE DEC B      ;
 $A9AF DEC B      ;
 $A9B0 DEC B      ;
 $A9B1 JP $A9FE   ;
